 "brief": "A ceiling hook for a hanging plant, PETG on FDM, printed on its side so the layers stack along Y. The ceiling is the plane z = 0 and the hook hangs below it inside x = -30 to 30, y = -15 to 15, z = -70 to 0. Two M4 wood screws go up into the ceiling at x = -15, y = -10 and y = +10, through a 6 mm plate. The pot hangs from a ring of 8 mm round wire that sits in the bottom of the hook at x = 0, z = -55 (the wire runs along Y there); the wire drops in down a 9 mm channel above it and comes in from the +X side through a 9 mm slot at z = -36 to -27, so the hook's tip rises on the +X side and the wire cannot slide out. The pot weighs 6 kg and hangs there for years; someone tugging or watering it pulls up to 2 g, up to 20 degrees off vertical. Safety factor 2.",
